<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Order of Amaranth

''The standing canon:'' convoys precious iron under ''the sign of the unfading flower'',
anointing cargo with amaranth-oil and putting rust-blooms down hard when a cache turns. Keepers
of the Unfading Seed. Amaranth churches — old ruined cathedrals, far-flung monasteries, pop-up
tent-churches — offer ''sanctuary; violence kapu''. Known for field medicine, sanctuary law, and
an unnerving ease around the free-willed dead. Elite shock troops and seekers of ancient ruins.
Management of the House of Masks, and its floor's neutrality, ride under their sign.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/livery>>

!! Livery & Sacrament

''The livery:'' amaranth ''wine-crimson into magenta'' over unbleached linen and bone-white.
Dried amaranth chaplets worn at the shoulder — ''unfading while everything iron around them
rusts'', which states the whole theology without a sermon. Deep agents carry
''tarnished-silver flower pins'': a flower that never fades, on a metal that does.

''The sacrament:'' ''amaranth-grain honey bread'', pressed and broken for guest-right and field
ration both — sanctuary law made edible. A traveler who has broken the Order's bread holds
guest-right at any tent-church that learns of it; the Order holds a long memory for who broke
bread and who refused it.

//(Gaia's dream-mirror carries the root: amarantos, "unfading" — and the grain pressed with
honey into sacred shapes, shared and eaten.)//

<<~/ahu>>

